WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.150
Find a position where the body can remain supported for a while.

2
00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:08.690
Lying down may be comfortable, or you can sit with the back and feet well supported.

3
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:13.310
Keep your eyes open if that helps you feel oriented.

4
00:00:15.010 --> 00:00:18.870
Nothing in this practice requires stillness; change position whenever you need to.

5
00:00:32.028 --> 00:00:35.338
Begin by noticing the whole shape of the body at once.

6
00:00:37.038 --> 00:00:38.768
Not every detail.

7
00:00:40.468 --> 00:00:45.208
Just the sense of a body here, taking up space, touching a surface, surrounded by air.

8
00:01:00.998 --> 00:01:03.228
Feel the places where weight is received.

9
00:01:04.928 --> 00:01:09.468
The back of the head, the shoulders, the back, the pelvis, the legs, or the feet.

10
00:01:11.168 --> 00:01:13.838
Let the supporting surface do its share of the work.

11
00:01:33.576 --> 00:01:35.936
Bring attention to the toes of the left foot.

12
00:01:37.636 --> 00:01:42.616
There may be warmth, coolness, pressure, tingling, pulsing, or no clear sensation.

13
00:01:44.316 --> 00:01:47.756
No sensation is also information.

14
00:01:49.456 --> 00:01:52.106
Include the sole, the heel, and the top of the foot.

15
00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:17.800
Notice the left ankle and lower leg.

16
00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.790
Feel the skin, the deeper weight, or the shape you know is there even when sensation is quiet.

17
00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:28.640
Move through the calf and shin toward the knee.

18
00:02:52.325 --> 00:02:54.225
Let the left knee be as it is.

19
00:02:55.925 --> 00:02:58.485
Notice the front, sides, and back of the joint.

20
00:03:00.185 --> 00:03:05.755
Then include the thigh, its contact with clothing or support, and the place where the leg meets the pelvis.

21
00:03:32.072 --> 00:03:35.852
Allow the whole left leg to be present at once, from hip to toes.

22
00:03:37.552 --> 00:03:40.062
You do not need to hold it in attention tightly.

23
00:03:41.762 --> 00:03:43.752
Let it rest in a wider field.

24
00:04:03.489 --> 00:04:04.849
Move to the toes of the right foot.

25
00:04:06.549 --> 00:04:09.059
Sense whatever is easiest to notice.

26
00:04:10.759 --> 00:04:12.119
The spaces between toes.

27
00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:14.429
The sole.

28
00:04:16.129 --> 00:04:16.879
The heel.

29
00:04:18.579 --> 00:04:19.539
The top of the foot.

30
00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:23.519
There is no need for the two sides to feel the same.

31
00:04:47.204 --> 00:04:49.684
Notice the right ankle, calf, and shin.

32
00:04:51.384 --> 00:04:56.154
Perhaps there are places that feel vivid and places that seem blank.

33
00:04:57.854 --> 00:04:58.664
Let both belong.

34
00:05:22.349 --> 00:05:24.469
Bring attention through the right knee and thigh.

35
00:05:26.169 --> 00:05:29.179
Notice pressure, temperature, fabric, or weight.

36
00:05:30.879 --> 00:05:33.539
Include the whole right leg from hip to toes.

37
00:05:59.856 --> 00:06:01.236
Feel both legs together.

38
00:06:02.936 --> 00:06:03.626
Their weight.

39
00:06:05.326 --> 00:06:05.956
Their length.

40
00:06:07.656 --> 00:06:08.896
Any difference between them.

41
00:06:10.596 --> 00:06:13.116
Let the next breath move while the legs remain supported.

42
00:06:39.432 --> 00:06:42.052
Bring attention to the pelvis and hips.

43
00:06:43.752 --> 00:06:47.892
Notice points of contact and the broad weight of this central part of the body.

44
00:06:49.592 --> 00:06:53.792
Sense the lower belly from the inside, without asking it to soften or change.

45
00:07:17.477 --> 00:07:19.437
The breath may create movement in the belly.

46
00:07:21.137 --> 00:07:24.807
Feel expansion, release, or very little movement.

47
00:07:26.507 --> 00:07:28.507
Let each breath have its own size.

48
00:07:54.824 --> 00:07:57.334
Move into the lower back.

49
00:07:59.034 --> 00:08:04.174
Perhaps you feel the support beneath it, the curve above it, or only a general area.

50
00:08:05.874 --> 00:08:09.974
Let attention include the sides of the waist and the whole lower torso.

51
00:08:33.659 --> 00:08:35.749
Notice the middle and upper back.

52
00:08:37.449 --> 00:08:43.109
Feel broad contact, individual points, warmth, coolness, ease, or effort.

53
00:08:44.809 --> 00:08:46.459
There is nothing to correct.

54
00:08:48.159 --> 00:08:54.199
If discomfort is asking for movement, adjust slowly and let the scan continue from the new position.

55
00:09:20.515 --> 00:09:23.015
Bring attention to the chest and ribs.

56
00:09:24.715 --> 00:09:27.565
Notice breathing from the front, sides, or back.

57
00:09:29.265 --> 00:09:32.515
The heart may be felt as a pulse, or it may not be noticeable.

58
00:09:34.215 --> 00:09:35.745
Do not search for it.

59
00:09:37.445 --> 00:09:38.995
Let the whole torso breathe.

60
00:10:07.943 --> 00:10:10.973
Now move to the fingers of the left hand.

61
00:10:12.673 --> 00:10:16.343
Feel fingertips, nails, palms, and the back of the hand.

62
00:10:18.043 --> 00:10:22.763
Notice whether the hand is open, curled, warm, cool, heavy, or light.

63
00:10:43.817 --> 00:10:45.747
Include the left wrist and forearm.

64
00:10:47.447 --> 00:10:50.397
Travel through the elbow and upper arm to the shoulder.

65
00:10:52.097 --> 00:10:54.497
Sense the whole arm resting in its position.

66
00:11:18.182 --> 00:11:20.522
Bring attention to the fingers of the right hand.

67
00:11:22.222 --> 00:11:25.182
Notice contact between fingers or with fabric.

68
00:11:26.882 --> 00:11:30.142
Feel the palm and back of the hand, then the wrist and forearm.

69
00:11:51.195 --> 00:11:54.065
Move through the right elbow and upper arm into the shoulder.

70
00:11:55.765 --> 00:11:59.375
Let both arms be present together, from shoulders to fingertips.

71
00:12:25.691 --> 00:12:27.451
Notice the shoulders.

72
00:12:29.151 --> 00:12:30.151
They do not have to drop.

73
00:12:31.851 --> 00:12:33.261
Simply feel their shape and weight.

74
00:12:34.961 --> 00:12:39.411
Include the places where the arms join the torso and the upper chest meets the neck.

75
00:13:03.096 --> 00:13:04.936
Bring attention to the throat and neck.

76
00:13:06.636 --> 00:13:09.926
Sense the front of the throat, the sides, and the back of the neck.

77
00:13:11.626 --> 00:13:12.846
Swallow if you need to.

78
00:13:14.546 --> 00:13:17.696
Let the jaw find a position that does not require extra holding.

79
00:13:41.381 --> 00:13:43.891
Feel the chin, lips, cheeks, and nose.

80
00:13:45.591 --> 00:13:48.081
Notice air at the nostrils if it is clear.

81
00:13:49.781 --> 00:13:53.871
Include the eyes resting in their sockets, the forehead, the temples, and the scalp.

82
00:14:22.819 --> 00:14:24.039
Notice the whole head.

83
00:14:25.739 --> 00:14:28.309
Sounds may be part of this moment too.

84
00:14:30.009 --> 00:14:33.509
Let hearing remain open while you sense the weight and temperature of the head.

85
00:14:59.826 --> 00:15:02.696
Now widen attention to include the entire body.

86
00:15:04.396 --> 00:15:08.646
Head, arms, torso, pelvis, legs, and feet.

87
00:15:10.346 --> 00:15:12.516
Some areas may be distinct and others vague.

88
00:15:14.216 --> 00:15:16.796
The body does not need to become one uniform feeling.

89
00:15:56.271 --> 00:15:58.151
Feel the body breathing as a whole.

90
00:15:59.851 --> 00:16:00.581
Breath entering.

91
00:16:02.281 --> 00:16:02.871
Breath leaving.

92
00:16:04.571 --> 00:16:09.961
Count three natural exhalations if that helps you remain here, then let go of the count.

93
00:16:49.436 --> 00:16:52.726
Notice that sensations change without asking permission.

94
00:16:54.426 --> 00:16:55.456
A pulse appears.

95
00:16:57.156 --> 00:16:58.536
Warmth spreads.

96
00:17:00.236 --> 00:17:01.956
An itch comes and goes.

97
00:17:03.656 --> 00:17:06.105
Stillness contains many small movements.

98
00:17:39.001 --> 00:17:42.511
If attention has wandered, receive the return without criticism.

99
00:17:44.211 --> 00:17:46.391
Come back to the broad contact with support.

100
00:17:48.091 --> 00:17:49.101
The whole body, here.

101
00:18:28.576 --> 00:18:30.886
Begin to recognize the room around the body.

102
00:18:32.586 --> 00:18:34.156
The air on exposed skin.

103
00:18:35.856 --> 00:18:37.796
Sounds near and far.

104
00:18:39.496 --> 00:18:42.406
Light through the eyelids or shapes in front of you.

105
00:19:08.723 --> 00:19:11.293
Invite a little movement into the fingers and toes.

106
00:19:12.993 --> 00:19:15.683
Rotate the wrists or ankles if that feels good.

107
00:19:17.383 --> 00:19:19.713
Stretch only in a way that suits your body today.

108
00:19:39.450 --> 00:19:43.580
Before changing position, notice one final time how the surface holds you.

109
00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:49.600
Then let the eyes open or refocus, and move at your own pace.

110
00:19:52.000 --> 00:19:53.500
The scan is complete.

111
00:19:55.200 --> 00:20:00.000
There was nothing particular you had to feel, and no state you had to achieve.
